sourceMaterials.text:
@amfonte @PayBox I never said the clip is a masterpiece. Compared to a human on the clock it is indeed good. One prompt, 15 minutes, from my phone. A person is not beating that combo by hand.

You keep answering a post I did not write and skipping the cost point every time.

I get your position though. If companies still have brains they will see it is early. But a jump like this already hints that the overall picture is not looking great.

@amfonte @PayBox True. However, what I am afraid of is that people will still treat this like the ultimate solution for everything. That is why sales will get rougher.

A lot of clients will sit on the idea that they can do it themselves, because some of the outputs already look good enough. If they hit that level on their own, they will not require any help.

EOD it is about businesses trying to decrease their burn rate and unnecessary costs.

@krealdesign @PayBox Fair. This one is a slop because the input was generic.

All it took - one prompt from my phone and a PayBox screenshot. I did not brief the product. The agent found the company and wrote the scenario itself.

Give it a tighter brief and it can pull stats and animate those too. Feed a full brand book and it stops looking like every other Opus stuff on X.
